cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, a citation is welcome and is not required (it is CC0)."
title: "Computing the conductor and index of orders generated by character values: an exact, dependency-free Python tool for SU(n), Sp(2m) and GL(n) (segmento.py)"
abstract: >-
  One file, Python 3 standard library only. Computes the conductor and the index of the ring
  generated by the character values of SU(n), Sp(2m) or GL(n) at an element of finite order, from
  the segment of eigenvalue exponents alone. Includes a filter for the primes that can divide the
  index that costs only divisibility, and a shortcut that computes the non-real index from the real one at half the
  degree. Declines, with a message, wherever the underlying notes mark a statement measured and
  not proved.
